{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for observability Draft1 exactbaa0e21e9ba65b643eb42ae485233dc9903f9b3f, primary notes/2026-10-12-observability-design.md.\n\n[P2] Define a real health/status read boundary (§4.5–4.6). Env has no canonical register selector; service binding supplies transport, not authority. Existing summary reads enforce signed/session permission, and chained register reads exclude summary. Specify the register ScopeRef and authorized bounded readiness observation/public exposure. sessions:true needs validated configuration (secret at least32 UTF8 bytes, valid deployment), not merely binding presence. Join throttling is not a limiter for every GET. Specify probe limits/timeouts/dependency failures. Summary has no outstanding-outbox count: status must use actual bounded outbox/duty/waiting reads, retain per-read heads/cursors/completeness, and never treat empty-but-next, denied or unknown as zero work. Preserve actual admin action requirements and latest1024-incident coverage.\n\n[P2] Allocate and validate the complete metric schema (§4.2–4.4). Five blobs/three doubles lack the promised request/trace correlation, restarts, timed attempts, wrote and multiple counts. Define per-kind slots/queries with stable meanings for every field. Native turn attempts differ from written timed entries; End includes idle/busy/clock-behind, while public answers separate unavailable reasons. Use fixed route templates and value allowlists, finite counts/write budgets, and meaningful tainted-value tests; a property-name denylist and100-character limit cannot prevent secrets in allowed values. Keep existing read-nothing diagnostics. Scope/timing correlation requires retention/access/cardinality boundaries, rather than a claim that absence of handles prevents profiling.\n\n[P2] Separate request identity and safe trace context (§4.4,6). A fresh server request ID cannot also be replaced by a caller's trace ID: one trace spans requests and caller IDs can collide. Keep server-minted request ID and validated non-authoritative trace/span IDs separate. Raw client tracestate is opaque text, so storing it in member-readable outbox/diagnosis violates the proposed text/secret privacy boundary. Define validation, malformed-input handling and selective trusted vendor-state retention/access or omission. Trace must not affect grants, idempotency or native answers. W3C defines trace IDs for a distributed trace and warns that opaque vendor state and malicious headers require privacy/parsing controls. [Trace Context](https://www.w3.org/TR/trace-context/)\n\n[P2] Resolve operational versus sealed persistence (§6). The draft says trace is not retained as input but adds it to a diagnosis entry. Current diagnosis is a sealed native Input with fixed schema; adding bytes affects hashes/replay. Keep correlation in an operational sidecar, or fully scope/version entry/outbox/transport/replay implications in the separate contract request. Do not describe this as only an optional Beside member. Missing, invalid, throwing or slow telemetry must leave results/delivery semantics unchanged, with bounded witnesses.\n\n[P2] Make the post-deploy gate truthful (§4.7,7). Specify sampled weighted error denominators/p95, fresh version/deployment/window, minimum observations/expected event kinds and no-data/stale/mixed-deployment/query-failure behavior. AE samples on write and read and exposes _sample_interval; multiplier1 and local error sampling bypass do not prove unsampled data. Use weighted aggregation and label coverage. AE also caps250 points per invocation, so sink overflow/drop handling needs a stated budget. [SQL API](https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/sql-api/) and [Limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/limits/). Calibration remains an observed future run; no figures are measured here. Extend recorded-SQL witnesses beyond threshold crossings to missing/stale/wrong-version and telemetry failures.\n\nArchitecture: reuse existing record/operator/outbox; repair unsupported reads, schema and persistence claims. Security: allowlisted operational data plus explicit trace/read authority boundaries are required. Simplification: one sink and native reads are a good direction once fields and coverage are explicit; complete scope remains, estimates only sequence it.\n\nValidation: primary13597B FULL Root/peers; both finals/audits and native fragment ledger FULL Root. Root independently verified selected whole-file and partial Source metadata/spans against013fac; no whole-source-survey/private woo claim. Root audit449B SHA5cf6f59086166739778c199928e2fa85cbede16f0b5012e4cbca722340cb003e. Official CF/W3C sources read separately. Prospective witnesses/calibration UNRUN; no Source/tests/gate/install/provider/browser/private reads. Design-only5a6/626 binding; no implementation, contract amendment, deployment or parent completion approved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:547bfae9b207f3e0a71c318346e10d504696c3a6","binding":"assigned","head":"baa0e21e9ba65b643eb42ae485233dc9903f9b3f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e20e54f4467471e669cd7a20aea908cc55e77e46\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6264f1e8e28666333a7c9564e5cb74a347b33a7c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a58ad94ee030d52d57d818c01d35151a09c4a02","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}